DESCRIPTION:<p>Set in 1940s Pittsburgh\, Wilson&rsquo\;s haunting drama fo
 llows blues musician Floyd &ldquo\;Schoolboy&rdquo\; Barton\, a man determ
 ined to win back the woman he loves and build a future beyond the limitati
 ons of Black life in America. As his friends gather and stories about Bart
 on flow\, what emerges is a richly layered portrait of masculinity and amb
 ition\, artistry\, community and the collective weight of dreams deferred.
