 llows blues musician Floyd &ldquo\;Schoolboy&rdquo\; Barton\, a man determ
 ined to win back the woman he loves and build a future beyond the limitati
 ons of Black life in America. As his friends gather and stories about Bart
 on flow\, what emerges is a richly layered portrait of masculinity and amb
 ition\, artistry\, community and the collective weight of dreams deferred.
 <br /><br />Santiago-Hudson&rsquo\;s celebrated history with Wilson&rsquo\
 ;s American Century Cycle\, including the Tony Award-winning&reg\; revival
  of <em>Jitney</em> and his most recent Tony nominated role as Bynum Walke
 r in <em>Joe Turner&rsquo\;s Come and Gone</em>\, brings decades of insigh
 t to this electrifying work.<br /><br />Leading support for August Wilson'
 s <em>Seven Guitars</em> is provided by Tracey T. Travis. Additional suppo
 rt is provided by the Samuel I. Newhouse Foundation.<br /><br />LCT season
  support is provided by Daryl Roth and American Airlines</p>
LOCATION:Lincoln Center Theater - Mitzi E. Newhouse\, 150 West 65th Street
 \, New York NY 10023
END:VEVENT
